<title>UK: ICO coffee exports top 81 mln in 12 months to May.</title>
<headline>ICO coffee exports top 81 mln in 12 months to May.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Coffee Organization (ICO) said on Monday producing members' exports reached 81.75 million 60-kg bags in the 12 months to May 1997, up sharply from 73.02 million in the same 1996 period.</p>
<p>In May, exports rose slightly to 7.03 million bags from 7.02 million in April. This compares with 6.60 million in May 1996.</p>
<p>In the first eight months of the current 1996/97 (Sept/Oct) coffee year to May, total exports were up at 57.36 million from 50.11 million in the same 1995/96 period.</p>
<p>Latest ICO export data, in thousand bags, included --</p>
<p>		     May 97     May 96  Oct/May 96/97   Oct/May</p>
<p>95/96</p>
<p>    Brazil	 1,580	 911	13,153	    7,257</p>
<p>    Colombia     1,139	 851	 7,911	    7,561</p>
<p>    Guatemala	406	 460	 3,664	    2,940</p>
<p>    El Salvador    278	  68	 2,409	    1,548</p>
<p>    Mexico	   274	 458	 3,982	    3,929</p>
<p>    Indonesia	457	 647	 3,165	    3,131</p>
<p>    Uganda	   193	 281	 3,137	    3,039</p>
<p>    Vietnam	  320	 286	 4,695	    3,257</p>
<p>    Ethiopia	 229	 194	 1,326	    1,002</p>
<p>    Ivory Coast    426	 270	 1,940	    1,821</p>
<p>    Kenya	    147	 177	   988	    1,128</p>
<p>    Costa Rica     138	 298	 1,446	    1,621</p>
<p>-- Jalil Hamid, London newsroom +44 171 542 4985</p>
